* `mulHeight₁_eq_places` — `mulHeight₁ x` is the product over the infinite places `v`, with
  multiplicity `v.mult`, of `max (v x) 1`, times the product over the finite places (Mathlib's
  `NumberField.mulHeight₁_eq`, restated).
* `mulHeight₁_eq_prod_embeddings` — for an algebraic integer, `mulHeight₁ x = ∏_σ max 1 ‖σ x‖`
  over the ring homomorphisms `σ : K →+* ℂ` (each real place is one of them, each complex place
  two, and every finite place gives the factor `1`).
* `mulHeight₁_two` — the normalization: `mulHeight₁ (2 : K) = 2 ^ [K:ℚ]`. So `mulHeight₁` is the
  height relative to `K`, the `[K:ℚ]`-th power of the absolute height (which is `2` at `2`).
* `mulHeight₁_half_rat` — the finite places count: `mulHeight₁ (1/2 : ℚ) = 2`, although
