* `mulHeight₁_zero_eq`, `mulHeight₁_one_eq` — the values at `0` and `1` are `1`, so the
  hypothesis `x ≠ 0` of statement 3 is needed to exclude `0`.
* `card_embeddings` — there are exactly `[K:ℚ]` ring homomorphisms `K →+* ℂ`, so
  `∑ σ : K →+* ℂ` is the sum over all `[K:ℚ]` conjugate embeddings.
* `rootOfUnity_iff_isOfFinOrder` — the right side of the uncompared equality case
  `HeightT2.sum_norm_sq_eq_mulHeight₁_sq_add_iff` is "`x` has finite multiplicative order", i.e.
  `x` is a root of unity.
* `mahlerMeasure_X_sub_C_eq`, `mahlerMeasure_X_sub_two`, `mahlerMeasure_eq_lead_mul_prod_roots` —
  `M(X − z) = max 1 ‖z‖`, so `M(X − 2) = 2`, and in general `M(p) = ‖lead p‖ · ∏ max 1 ‖α‖` over
  the roots with multiplicity (Jensen's formula, Mathlib's theorem restated).
* `minpoly_eq_zero_of_not_isIntegral` — `minpoly ℤ x` is `0` (a junk value) when `x` is not
